· A4 — Initial viability. X(0)\in\mathcal{V}.
· A5 — Smoothness. K:[0,1]\to[0,1] and \Phi:[0,1]\to[0,1] are twice continuously differentiable with K'>0 strictly? In main, K strictly decreasing so K'<0. We assume K(0)=1, K'<0, K''\ge 0 for simplicity. \Phi(0)=0, \Phi(1)=1, \Phi'>0, \Phi''\le 0.
· A6 — Latency critical set. The set \mathcal{J}_c is determined by the physical latency condition and is fixed.

