Appendix G. Pre-Registered Simulation Protocol

This appendix describes the future computational evaluation. No simulations are run in this draft. All parameters and code will be pre-registered before any full Monte Carlo run.

G.1 Simulation Model

We implement the multilayer Markov jump process defined in Section 5 and Appendix D.

State vector:

s(t)=(s_{i,j}(t))\in\{0,1\}^{N\times 8}.

Transition rates:

· Exogenous failure: \lambda_{i,j}.
· Repair: \eta_{i,j}.
· Endogenous propagation: as defined in Section D.1.

Architecture parameters:

· Centralized benchmark: \Phi_j=0 for all j, A=0 for non-critical functions.
· Fractal architecture: \Phi_j=\Phi^* for latency-critical functions, A optimized for non-critical functions.
· Hybrid: intermediate values.

G.2 Numerical Algorithm: Gillespie Stochastic Simulation

We use the standard Gillespie algorithm for continuous-time Markov chains:

1. Initialize state s(0)=s_0.
2. Compute all transition rates \lambda_k(s) for the current state.
3. Compute total rate \Lambda_{\text{tot}}=\sum_k \lambda_k(s).
4. Sample time to next event: \Delta t\sim \operatorname{Exp}(\Lambda_{\text{tot}}).
5. Choose event k with probability \lambda_k/\Lambda_{\text{tot}}.
6. Update state s\mapsto s+e_k (where e_k is the change vector).
7. Record X(t) and check viability.
8. Stop if X(t)\notin\mathcal{V} or t>T; otherwise return to step 2.

Pseudocode:

```
function simulate(T, s0, params):
    t = 0
    s = s0
    while t < T:
        compute rates = [λ1, λ2, ..., λK] for state s
        Λ = sum(rates)
        if Λ == 0:
            break
        Δt = expovariate(Λ)
        if t + Δt > T:
            break
        choose event with prob rates/Λ
        update s
        t += Δt
        if X(s) not in V:
            return False
    return True
```

