G.4 Statistical Analysis

For each scenario s, compute

\Delta_s
=
R_{\text{fractal}}^{(s)}
-
R_{\text{central}}^{(s)}.

Primary criterion: At least 4 of 5 scenario-specific one-sided 95% bootstrap confidence intervals for \Delta_s have lower bound greater than 0.

Secondary criterion: The lower bound of a one-sided 95% confidence interval for a random-effects pooled mean of \Delta_s is greater than 0.

Bootstrap procedure:

1. For each Monte Carlo run, record the binary outcome (viable / not viable).
2. Compute the observed resilience \hat R.
3. Resample the binary outcomes with replacement 10,000 times.
4. Compute the distribution of \Delta under the resampling.
5. Use the 5th percentile of the bootstrap distribution as the lower bound of the one-sided 95% CI.

