Appendix H. Additional Technical Lemmas

H.1 Perron–Frobenius Monotonicity

Lemma H.1

Let A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n} be nonnegative matrices with A\le B entrywise. Then

\rho(A)\le \rho(B).

Proof.
For any \varepsilon>0, B+\varepsilon J is primitive, where J is the all-ones matrix. By the Perron–Frobenius theorem for primitive matrices, \rho(A+\varepsilon J)\le \rho(B+\varepsilon J). Taking \varepsilon\to 0 gives \rho(A)\le \rho(B). \square

H.2 Concavity of Spectral Radius?

The spectral radius of a nonnegative matrix is not generally concave in its entries. However, in our case the benefit function B(\bar A) is linear in \Phi(\bar A), and \Phi is concave, so B is concave. We do not require concavity of the spectral radius itself.

H.3 Smoothness of the Viability Score

Under Assumptions A5, the architectural score

V(\bar A)=B(\bar A)-\kappa D(\bar A)

is twice continuously differentiable, and

V''(\bar A)=\beta \Phi''(\bar A)-\kappa D''(\bar A).

If \Phi''<0 and D''>0, then V''<0, so V is strictly concave.

