2. Mean-field error bounds. Derive explicit constants in the O(1/\sqrt{n}) error bound for the sparse random graph limit. Use coupling and martingale methods.
3. Nonlinear delay stability. Extend the Lyapunov–Krasovskii approach to sector-bounded nonlinearities and derive less conservative delay-dependent stability conditions.
4. Multilayer percolation phase transitions. Determine the critical tolerance \alpha_c below which the multilayer network undergoes a first-order (abrupt) transition, and show that fractal architecture shifts the transition toward second-order (continuous) percolation.
5. Governance as a strategic game. Model governance not merely as consensus but as a game among strategic actors with local preferences and incentives. Investigate whether the latency hierarchy induces stable coalitions.
6. Resource-cost functions. Specify explicit engineering forms for e_i and m_i and derive the resulting optimization problem.
7. Pre-registered simulation. Implement the full simulation architecture described in Appendix G and run the pre-registered experiments.

